The template sheets in this directory (hyle-all-templates.zip) and the manifests generated from
them (*-manifest.json) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0-1.0. The full text is in
../../LICENSES/CC0-1.0.txt. Whatever you draw on a template is yours, with no conditions from us.

Exception: the `reference_delete_me` layer in each Hiragana, Katakana, Devanagari, Naskh and
Nastaliq sheet holds glyph outlines copied from a Noto font (Noto Sans JP for Hiragana and
Katakana, Noto Sans Devanagari for Devanagari, Noto Naskh Arabic for Naskh, Noto Nastaliq Urdu
for Nastaliq), licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1, not CC0. Their copyright
lines and the full licence text are in OFL.txt, beside this file. That layer is there only to
position your drawing; HOW_TO_USE.md tells you to delete it before export, so what you actually
draw carries no conditions from us or from Noto.

The generator scripts here (*.py) are engine code, licensed Apache-2.0 as their SPDX lines say.
